---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { person } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="How Raphael Ugwu works: developer-focused documentation, docs-as-code, and close collaboration with engineering and product."
  current="about"
>
  <article>
    <header class="article-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="article-summary">
        I'm Raphael. I've been writing for developers since 2017, first as a developer advocate in Lagos and now as a
        senior technical writer in Toronto.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I love working on developer-focused docs: API references, quick starts, how-to guides, and tutorials. I
        trained as an electrical engineer and I write JavaScript and Python, so I read the code to confirm how a
        feature behaves before I describe it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do my best work alongside engineering, product, and customer success teams, keeping a product's whole
        documentation set accurate and current. I enjoy tinkering with API doc tools and cleaning up outdated doc
        sets. Lately that means building AI-assisted workflows that let one writer cover what used to need a team.
      </p>

      <h2>My ideal work environment</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Short version.</strong> Have me own a product or process and trust me to get the work done.
        Communicate proactively with me (I'll always reach out first) and tell me when I'm doing well or need to
        improve. Give me room to advocate for the developers who use the product and to solve their pain points.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Long version.</strong> I do my best work in organisations where I'm trusted to get the job done in
        the most efficient way. I prefer a hands-off management style: a manager who works on the broader roadmap
        with me, shares feedback, and gives constructive criticism.
      </p>
      <p>
        I appreciate organisations where frequent, two-way communication is the norm. I like a healthy amount of
        ownership over my work and product area, and I don't mind taking on tasks outside my core job description
        when they help the organisation's mission.
      </p>

      <h2>What colleagues get from me</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A bridge between engineering, design, product, marketing, and support. I'm good at getting colleagues to
          see things from the developer's perspective.
        </li>
        <li>Someone who thrives in a remote, asynchronous environment.</li>
        <li>Experience managing open source documentation content and its contributors.</li>
        <li>Experience running online developer communities and supporting the developers in them.</li>
        <li>A steady hand on projects like documentation updates and migrations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reach out</h2>
      <p>
        Email me at <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a>, or find me on {
          person.links.map((link, i) => (
            <>
              {i > 0 && ' and '}
              <a href={link.url}>{link.label}</a>
            </>
          ))
        }.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
